BT
/F2 14 Tf 50 750 Td (Scalable Fault-Tolerant Quantum Surface Codes with Low Overhead) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 728 Td (Abstract) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 50 712 Td (Surface codes offer a promising route to scalable quantum computing. Here we demonstrate a logical error rate reduction using adaptive syndrome decoding [1].) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 698 Td (Introduction) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 50 682 Td (Quantum error correction preserves logical qubits against decoherence [2]. Recent topological architectures achieve fault tolerance below a physical error rate of 1 percent [1], [3].) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 50 668 Td (Syndrome measurement schedules must minimize crosstalk [4]. Our architecture reduces physical qubit overhead by 34 percent compared to standard planar layouts [1].) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 654 Td (Methods) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 50 638 Td (We simulated a rotated surface code lattice with code distances d = 3, 5, and 7 using minimum-weight perfect matching decoders [3].) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 624 Td (Results) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 50 608 Td (Logical error suppression scales exponentially with code distance d when physical error is 0.001 [2]. Threshold analysis confirms stability across 1000 syndrome cycles [4].) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 50 594 Td (References) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 50 578 Td ([1] Fowler, A. G., et al. \(2012\). Surface codes: Towards practical large-scale quantum computation. Physical Review A, 86\(3\), 032324. DOI: 10.1103/PhysRevA.86.032324) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 50 564 Td ([2] Shor, P. W. \(1995\). Scheme for reducing decoherence in quantum computer memory. Physical Review A, 52\(4\), R2493. DOI: 10.1103/PhysRevA.52.R2493) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 50 550 Td ([3] Dennis, E., et al. \(2002\). Topological quantum memory. Journal of Mathematical Physics, 43\(9\), 4452-4505. DOI: 10.1063/1.1499754) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 50 536 Td ([4] Bravyi, S., and Kitaev, A. \(1998\). Quantum codes on a lattice with boundary. arXiv:quant-ph/9811052. DOI: 10.48550/arXiv.quant-ph.9811052) Tj
